### Graduation Project Tracker: manual API tests (VS Code REST Client)
### Locally the Turnstile TEST secret accepts the dummy token "XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX".
@api = http://localhost:3000/api
@turnstile = XXXX.DUMMY.TOKEN.XXXX

### Health check
GET {{api}}/health

### Register a student (201)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{turnstile}}

{ "name": "Test Student", "email": "student1@example.edu", "password": "Password123!" }

### Register trying to become admin (400, field not allowed)
POST {{api}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{turnstile}}

{ "name": "Sneaky", "email": "sneaky@example.edu", "password": "Password123!", "role": "admin" }

### Log in (200, copy the token into @token below)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
X-Turnstile-Token: {{turnstile}}

{ "email": "student1@example.edu", "password": "Password123!" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### Current user (200)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Current user without token (401)
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Supervisors for the drop-down (200)
GET {{api}}/supervisors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Register a project (201) - set supervisorId to a real supervisor id
POST {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Smart Attendance System",
  "description": "Face recognition attendance for lecture halls.",
  "teamName": "Team Falcon",
  "repoUrl": "https://github.com/example/smart-attendance",
  "supervisorId": 1
}

### Register a second project with the same student (409)
POST {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Another", "description": "Second project attempt.", "teamName": "Team B", "supervisorId": 1 }

### Invalid project: title too short, bad repo link (400)
POST {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Hi", "description": "Too short title test.", "teamName": "T1", "repoUrl": "http://evil.example", "supervisorId": 1 }

### Sending status from the client (400, field not allowed)
POST {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Approved already", "description": "Trying to set the status.", "teamName": "Team C", "supervisorId": 1, "supervisionStatus": "accepted" }

### Not JSON (415)
POST {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: text/plain

hello

### List my projects (200)
GET {{api}}/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Search with SQL characters (200, treated as plain text)
GET {{api}}/projects?search=' OR 1=1 --
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid status filter (400)
GET {{api}}/projects?status=approved
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Another team's project (404): use an id that belongs to a different team
GET {{api}}/projects/999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
